CONTEXT.md:120: ## Force-Kill Undo
CONTEXT.md-121- A panic-button action that warns the developer, forcefully terminates currently running agent subprocesses, reverts all model changes made during the current loop run, and interrupts the loop so the developer can revise the requirements or decisions before continuing. It preserves unrelated developer edits that existed before the loop run began.
